    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a30ddce_00a6bc52",
        "filename": "keystone/common/policies/base.py",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 10608
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-09T14:09:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we\u0027ve gone a little crazy with these policy rules that have long names and are never checked directly. As an operator, it would be much easier to have fewer rules and read a check_str for the API I\u0027m trying to call that does the AND\u0027ing, OR\u0027ing, NOT\u0027ing, etc... so I don\u0027t have to go lookup \u0027service_admin_or_token_subject\u0027, then go lookup \u0027service_or_admin\u0027, etc. I\u0027d be fine cleaning that up in a later patch, though, if need be.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "feb1ab82440531c590c65b32b0cdfd1f16db008c",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a30ddce_4080b4c0",
        "filename": "keystone/common/policies/base.py",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 10608
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-09T14:09:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the current system, the \u0027default\u0027 rule is checked by oslo.policy when the rule that it was told to check is not found. Once all policy defaults are in code, that will never be possible anymore, making the \u0027default\u0027 rule obsolete. So it\u0027s not needed here... just leave it in the policy.json file, and when that file is deleted it would just go away.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "feb1ab82440531c590c65b32b0cdfd1f16db008c",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
